==English==
[[Image:Bowler Hat sw (fcm).jpg|thumb|A bowler (hat)]]

===Etymology===
From the name of the hatmakers Thomas and William Bowler, associated with early production.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[hard]] [[round]] [[black]] [[felt]] [[hat]] with a [[narrow]] [[brim]], formerly worn by men.
#: {{syn|en|bowler|derby<q:US>}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=22 March 2012|author=Scott Tobias|work=AV Club|title=Cabin Boy|url=http://www.avclub.com/articles/cabin-boy,71269/|passage=It takes a special arrogance to snort at an oral report on the origins (and proper tipping) of the '''bowler hat''', but there’s Nathanial, giggling his way through the presentation before offering up his report on the more rarefied 14th-century Norwegian derby.}}

